#!/usr/bin/env -S dotnet fsi scripts/pre-push.fsx
// The git hook entry point: scripts/pre-push.fsx does the work, this only names it. git runs a hook as a
// file called `pre-push` from the top of the working tree, `dotnet fsi` runs only files ending in .fsx, and a
// shebang line is the one place a script can say "run this other file". Run `dotnet fsi scripts/install-hooks.fsx`
// to link it into .git/hooks.
